<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116375" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡρόνομ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hour-divider,</i>
			i.e. <i>a dial</i> or <i>clock,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				14.6
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡρόμαντις.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Astrology, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡροσκόπος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11.1
			</span></i>, <i>ascendant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Man.
				1.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				262
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Doroth.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
			</span></i> Astr.<i><span class="en">
				2.24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> name of
			certain deities, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δεκαδάρχαι καὶ ζῳδιοκράτορες καὶ
					ὡρονόμοι καὶ κραταιοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					351
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
